{
  "title": "Normalize: store a text import's original text so Re-extract works for it",
  "description": "The reextract normalize op rebuilds a recipe from its stored source: the fetched page (fetch_html step output) for scrapes and captures, or the extracted recipe (extract_recipe output) for Paprika and photo imports. \
Recipes created from pasted text (POST /api/import/text, then POST /api/recipes) never run a job and store neither the text nor the extracted recipe, so GET /api/recipes/normalize-ops reports reextract unavailable for them ('Recipe has no saved source to re-extract from'). \
Store the original text when a text-imported recipe is saved (e.g. pass it through CreateRecipeRequest and record it as a source the reextract op can read, such as a job with an extract_recipe output or a dedicated table), then teach scraping::stored_source and the reextract job setup to re-run text extraction (or just re-parse) from it. \
Photo imports could likewise re-run vision extraction from their stored photos instead of only re-parsing the stored extract. \
Both clients send the text already; only the create call needs the extra field. \
API tests first, no data/ diffs expected.",
